  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.55,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R36"],
      "pins": ["R36.1", "R36.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTN", "VOUTP"],
      "observed": "R36 carries the schematic value \"24k\" (and the SPICE deck models it as 24k), but its MPN is \"FRC0805J240TSD\" and its description/ki fields state \"24Ω\" (the 3-digit code 240 = 24 Ω). It sits as a shunt directly between VOUTP and VOUTN, the protected motor rail (which also carries a SMAJ60A TVS and a 28 V zener clamp).",
      "expected": "For a bleeder/shunt across a tens‑of‑volts motor rail the intended part is the 24 kΩ indicated by the value field and SPICE (≈mA at 24 V, within the 0805 125 mW rating). A 24 Ω part (per the MPN/description) would draw ~1–2 A and dissipate tens of watts, which is impossible for an 0805 125 mW resistor and would load/short the rail. The value, MPN, description and role must agree.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"R36\") (value \"24k\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\") ... (field (name \"Description\") \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"220\") (name \"VOUTP\") ... (node (ref \"R36\") (pin \"2\") ...)) (net (code \"219\") (name \"VOUTN\") ... (node (ref \"R36\") (pin \"1\") ...))"},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "R36 VOUTN VOUTP 24k"}
      ],
      "impact": "If the board is assembled from the MPN/description (24 Ω) instead of the schematic value (24 kΩ), R36 becomes a low‑ohmic shunt across the motor rail, drawing excessive current and overheating the 0805 part while loading the rail, so the board behaves differently from the intended high‑impedance bleeder.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Every component and connection the specification explicitly calls out (16 MHz Y1/Y2 on U8/U9, isolated CAN transceivers U10/U11, LTC4412 U6, SN74LVC1G07 e‑stop buffers U15/U22/U35/U36 feeding ESTOP_OUT on J2/J13, CDSOT23‑SM712 D9/D10 on the CAN pairs, GLOBAL_EN tied only to SW1) matches the netlist, and the documented open issues (C5 footprint, USB diode, LED polarity, etc.) are present as expected. The one internal inconsistency is R36, whose MPN/description specify a 24 Ω part while its schematic value and SPICE model are 24 kΩ; 24 Ω is electrically impossible as a shunt across the motor rail, indicating a wrong‑value/sourcing anomaly."
}

